---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const brandMarkup = `/* brand.css — imported AFTER the framework, outside any @layer,
   so it wins by the cascade contract. Re-skin by remapping the SEMANTIC
   tier only — never touch component files.

   THE DARK RULE: an unlayered :root declaration beats the framework's
   LAYERED [data-theme="dark"] remap of the same token. So every token you
   set on :root must be re-set in your own dark block if dark differs —
   otherwise your light value leaks into dark mode. */
:root {
  --bo-color-accent: #0f766e;        /* your brand teal */
  --bo-color-accent-strong: #115e59;
  --bo-color-accent-solid: #0f766e;  /* must keep >= 4.5:1 under white text */
  --bo-color-accent-subtle: #f0fdfa;
  --bo-color-accent-text: #115e59;   /* >= 4.5:1 on accent-subtle */
  /* A full accent swap also includes the accent-adjacent tokens the
     framework colors blue by default: */
  --bo-color-focus-ring: #0d9488;    /* else focus rings stay blue */
  --bo-color-bg-selected: #f0fdfa;   /* else selected rows stay blue */
  --bo-font-sans: "Your Corporate Sans", system-ui, sans-serif;
  --bo-radius-md: 0.25rem;           /* sharper corporate corners */
}

[data-theme="dark"] {
  --bo-color-accent: #14b8a6;        /* REQUIRED: re-set every :root token */
  --bo-color-accent-text: #5eead4;   /* light step for dark surfaces */
  --bo-color-accent-subtle: #134e4a;
  --bo-color-bg-selected: #134e4a;
}`;
---
<Gallery title="Theming guide">
  <p class="demo-note">
    Re-skin the whole framework by remapping the <strong>semantic token tier</strong> in
    your own unlayered stylesheet — the cascade contract guarantees it wins. Never
    override component classes; never touch the raw palette tier.
   Ready-made palettes ship — see the <a href={base + '/base/palettes'}>Palettes reference</a>.</p>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The contract</h2>
    <ul class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight" style="padding-inline-start: 1.25rem">
      <li><strong>Remap semantic tokens only</strong> (<code>--bo-color-*</code>, fonts, radii). Component-local tokens (<code>--bo-btn-*</code>) are for per-instance tweaks, not brand.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep the token roles honest</strong>: <code>*-solid</code> carries white text in both themes (≥ 4.5:1); <code>*-text</code> sits on <code>*-subtle</code> (≥ 4.5:1); dark mode remaps <code>*-text</code>/<code>*-subtle</code>, never <code>*-solid</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Verify contrast when you swap hues</strong> — the roles encode the ratios, your values must honor them.</li>
      <li><strong>The dark rule</strong>: unlayered <code>:root</code> beats the framework's <em>layered</em> dark remaps — every token you set must be re-set in your own <code>[data-theme="dark"]</code> block if dark differs.</li>
      <li><strong>An accent swap is a family swap</strong>: <code>accent</code>, <code>accent-strong</code>, <code>accent-solid</code>, <code>accent-subtle</code>, <code>accent-text</code>, plus <code>focus-ring</code> and <code>bg-selected</code> — miss one and the UI is two-toned.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>brand.css</h2>
    <pre><code>{brandMarkup}</code></pre>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>A real, shipped preset — <code>@busy-office/ui/css/brand-indigo</code></h2>
    <p>Not just this page's prose example — an actual importable file
    (<code>packages/core/src/css/brand/brand-indigo.css</code>), validated by the
    same contrast gate as the base theme (<code>scripts/check-contrast.mjs</code>
    now checks every file in <code>src/css/brand/</code>, not asserted by hand).
    The live preview below applies the identical token values scoped to just this
    box (for a real app, they'd go on <code>:root</code> as shown above — this
    page keeps its own default teal everywhere else on purpose):</p>
    <div class="brand-preview" style="padding: var(--bo-space-4); border: 1px solid var(--bo-color-border-default); border-radius: var(--bo-radius-md); display: flex; gap: var(--bo-space-2); align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
      <button class="bo-btn">Approve</button>
      <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary">Cancel</button>
      <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--accent">In review</span>
      <a href="#" class="bo-u-text-muted" style="color: var(--bo-color-accent)">A link, for focus-ring/link-color coverage</a>
    </div>
    <style>
      .brand-preview {
        --bo-color-accent: #4338ca;
        --bo-color-accent-strong: #3730a3;
        --bo-color-accent-solid: #4338ca;
        --bo-color-accent-subtle: #eef2ff;
        --bo-color-accent-text: #3730a3;
        --bo-color-focus-ring: #4f46e5;
        --bo-color-bg-selected: #eef2ff;
      }
      [data-theme="dark"] .brand-preview {
        --bo-color-accent: #818cf8;
        --bo-color-accent-strong: #a5b4fc;
        --bo-color-accent-solid: #4f46e5;
        --bo-color-accent-subtle: #312e81;
        --bo-color-accent-text: #c7d2fe;
        --bo-color-focus-ring: #818cf8;
        --bo-color-bg-selected: #312e81;
      }
    </style>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Switching themes at runtime</h2>
    <p>Flip <code>data-theme</code> on the root. One catch: a component's
    <code>background-color</code> transition animates on the switch while the text
    <code>color</code> snaps instantly, so text can flash on a still-light background
    (near-invisible going to dark). Freeze transitions for the one frame of the flip
    with <code>data-bo-theming</code> (shipped in the utilities layer):</p>
    <pre><code>{`function setTheme(value) {
  const html = document.documentElement;
  html.setAttribute('data-bo-theming', '');   // freeze transitions
  html.dataset.theme = value;
  requestAnimationFrame(() =>
    requestAnimationFrame(() => html.removeAttribute('data-bo-theming')));
}`}</code></pre>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Two frames: one to paint the new theme with transitions
    off, the next to re-enable them. Hover/focus transitions are unaffected.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Versioning policy</h2>
    <p>Semantic tokens, documented class names, and <code>data-*</code>/ARIA contracts
    are the public API — breaking any of them is a major version. Component-internal
    selectors and the raw palette are not API. <strong>Per-component dist file
    placement is explicitly not API until v1.0</strong> — granular importers should
    pin versions; moves are recorded in the CHANGELOG. New components/tokens are
    minors; visual-only tweaks within the same contracts are patches.</p>
  </section>
  <Related links={[["/concepts/cascade", "Cascade contract"], ["/base/colors", "Colors & tokens"], ["/getting-started/versioning", "Versioning"]]} />
</Gallery>
